262
00:24:05.714 --> 00:24:08.551
Events for facts, sync APIs for queries.

263
00:24:08.831 --> 00:24:09.962
Across the fleet.

264
00:24:10.242 --> 00:24:11.117
Question:

265
00:24:11.397 --> 00:24:12.890
How is failure contained?

266
00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:14.301
Typical choice:

267
00:24:14.581 --> 00:24:15.946
Cells at large scale.

268
00:24:16.226 --> 00:24:17.229
Front ends.

269
00:24:17.509 --> 00:24:18.383
Question:

270
00:24:18.663 --> 00:24:20.199
How do clients get data?

271
00:24:20.479 --> 00:24:21.610
Typical choice:

272
00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:25.709
BFF per client; micro-frontends if many UI teams.

273
00:24:27.059 --> 00:24:29.107
A common, healthy evolution path:

274
00:24:29.387 --> 00:24:31.520
Layered monolith, ship the product.

275
00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:40.120
Modular monolith with hexagonal modules, as the domain grows, draw context boundaries (Ch 33) and enforce them.

276
00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:48.507
Selective extraction, pull out the modules with real drivers (scaling, cadence, team) into services, connected by events.

277
00:24:48.787 --> 00:24:53.309
Cells, when blast radius, not code structure, becomes the dominant risk.

278
00:24:54.659 --> 00:24:57.006
Each step keeps the previous one's discipline.

279
00:24:57.286 --> 00:25:05.862
Skipping step 2, going straight from a tangled monolith to microservices, produces the distributed monolith of §1.1.

