00:26:52.749 --> 00:26:54.029
Accepted, Authors:

316
00:26:54.309 --> 00:26:56.143
Principal engineers, Reviewers:

317
00:26:56.423 --> 00:26:59.538
SRE, all tech leads, finance (cost of cells).

318
00:26:59.818 --> 00:27:13.194
Context, A layered monolith that tangled, then 26 entity services with 9-hop checkout calls, then a festival outage in which one city's surge took every city down through shared Kafka and DB pools.

319
00:27:13.474 --> 00:27:33.399
Decision, Combine styles by level: hexagonal inside deployables; modular monolith for Ordering + Catalog; services for Inventory and Fulfilment; events between contexts; 8 cells by city group with a global router and control plane; BFF per client; serverless for bursty side jobs.

320
00:27:34.749 --> 00:27:54.248
Related ADRs, ADR-200 Hexagonal package structure + ArchUnit dependency rule (L1); ADR-201 Ordering + Catalog modular monolith with Spring Modulith verification; ADR-202 Extract only with a named driver (scaling, cadence,

321
00:27:54.528 --> 00:28:19.488
team) (L2); ADR-203 No required synchronous chains longer than 2 hops on checkout; ADR-204 Cells by city group, at most 15% of customers per cell (L3); ADR-205 Deploy waves: canary cell, 12 h spacing for high-risk changes, per-cell flags (L3); ADR-206 Tenant move protocol: hold, copy, flip, verify,

322
00:28:19.768 --> 00:28:28.643
drop, CDC pre-copy for large cities (L4); ADR-207 Serverless for invoice PDFs and image processing.

323
00:28:28.923 --> 00:28:29.883
Requirements.

324
00:28:31.233 --> 00:28:33.003
R1, Blast radius.

325
00:28:33.283 --> 00:28:39.150
No single infrastructure failure or city surge may affect more than 15% of customers.

326
00:28:39.430 --> 00:28:48.347
R2, Checkout latency. p99 300 ms at festival peak; at most 2 required synchronous hops on the checkout path.

327
00:28:48.627 --> 00:28:50.249
R3, Testability.

328
00:28:50.529 --> 00:28:56.075
Business rules testable without infrastructure; the full domain suite runs in under a minute.

329
00:28:56.355 --> 00:28:57.763
R4, Safe change.

330
00:28:58.043 --> 00:29:02.011
A bad deploy that triggers within 12 hours affects at most one cell.

331
00:29:03.361 --> 00:29:05.175
R5, Safe rebalancing.

332
00:29:05.455 --> 00:29:08.868
Moving a city between cells loses no acknowledged write.

333
00:29:09.148 --> 00:29:10.556
Decisions in detail.

334
00:29:10.836 --> 00:29:13.524
Inside deployables (ADR-200).

335
00:29:13.804 --> 00:29:22.060
Domain or application or adapter packages; ArchUnit rules fail the build on infrastructure types in the domain (L1).

336
00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:26.031
Modules first (ADR-201 or 202).

337
00:29:26.311 --> 00:29:32.284
Ordering and Catalog stay together; Inventory and Fulfilment extracted for flash-sale scaling.

338
00:29:32.564 --> 00:29:38.409
Every extraction ADR names its driver and the latency or availability cost (L2).

339
00:29:39.759 --> 00:29:41.850
Cells (ADR-204).

340
00:29:42.130 --> 00:29:52.605
8 cells; router with replicated table at every edge; control plane may be down without affecting the data plane; national reporting via CDC into the lakehouse.

341
00:29:52.885 --> 00:29:55.210
Deploys (ADR-205).

342
00:29:55.490 --> 00:30:03.853
Canary cell first; normal changes roll within a day; high-risk changes 12 h per wave; kill-switch flags per cell (L3).

343
00:30:04.133 --> 00:30:06.650
City moves (ADR-206).

344
00:30:06.930 --> 00:30:16.743
Hold, copy, flip, verify, drop; cities over 1M carts pre-copied via CDC so the hold covers only the final delta (L4).

345
00:30:18.093 --> 00:30:19.117
Consequences.

346
00:30:19.397 --> 00:30:31.707
Roughly 1.6x infrastructure cost for cells (duplicated DBs, Kafka, caches), a router and control plane to build and operate, and slower rollouts for risky changes.

347
00:30:31.987 --> 00:30:39.837
In return, the festival scenario becomes a one-cell incident, and checkout no longer depends on nine services being up.

