00:35:44.095 --> 00:35:51.007
MODULAR MONOLITH versus MICROSERVICES: what a module boundary costs when it becomes a network boundary.

398
00:35:51.287 --> 00:35:57.239
A checkout needs five. collaborators (catalog, pricing, inventory, promotions, orders).

399
00:35:57.519 --> 00:36:00.463
The SAME collaborator logic is called three ways:

400
00:36:03.313 --> 00:36:04.230
On screen:

401
00:36:04.510 --> 00:36:07.347
One checkout = 5 collaborator calls.

402
00:36:07.627 --> 00:36:11.041
Same logic, same responses (verified identical).

403
00:36:11.321 --> 00:36:47.603
3,000 measured runs each, localhost. deployment p50 p99 p50 versus modules. modular monolith (in-process calls) 11.2 µs 30.7 µs 1x. microservices, 5 serial HTTP calls 1107.2 µs 7825.5 µs 99x. microservices, 5 parallel HTTP calls 484.1 µs 4500.1 µs 43x.

404
00:36:47.883 --> 00:36:57.291
Availability if every deployable is 99.9% and all are required on the checkout. path: modular monolith (1 deployable):

405
00:36:57.571 --> 00:37:05.165
99.900%, then 43 min per month down. microservices (6 deployables):

406
00:37:05.445 --> 00:37:10.736
99.401%, then 259 min per month down.

407
00:37:11.016 --> 00:37:12.531
The rest is in the chapter.

408
00:37:15.381 --> 00:37:29.205
Reading it: ~11 µs in-process versus ~1.1 ms serial HTTP (~99x), on localhost, the best case: no real network, no TLS, no service mesh.

409
00:37:29.485 --> 00:37:31.021
Fan-out roughly halves it.

410
00:37:31.301 --> 00:37:34.565
Absolute numbers vary per run; the ratio is stable.

411
00:37:34.845 --> 00:37:39.965
In absolute terms ~1 ms is small against a 300 ms budget.

412
00:37:40.245 --> 00:37:57.013
What bites is the tail (p99 already in milliseconds before any real network or GC) and availability: six required 99.9% deployables expect 259 minutes per month of downtime versus 43 for one.

413
00:37:58.363 --> 00:38:12.037
The decision rule follows: keep modules in-process unless a concrete driver (scaling, cadence, ownership) justifies the price, and when you extract, remove required synchronous hops rather than chaining them.

414
00:38:13.387 --> 00:38:15.691
