765
01:06:13.528 --> 01:06:20.717
(B3) In L3, add a bad config push incident type that deploys to all cells at once (bypassing waves).

766
01:06:20.997 --> 01:06:23.301
How much of the cells' benefit does it erase?

767
01:06:23.581 --> 01:06:25.843
What does that tell you about config pipelines?

768
01:06:27.193 --> 01:06:37.347
(B4) Extend L4 with a CDC-style pre-copy: stream writes to the target cell while still serving from the source, then hold only for the final delta.

769
01:06:37.627 --> 01:06:41.617
Compare hold durations for a city with 100x more data.

770
01:06:41.897 --> 01:06:52.905
(B4) Write the ADR for introducing cells to your own system: drivers, partition key, cell size, router design, wave policy, cost estimate and revisit trigger.

